### =========================================================================
### 🎓 USER ENUMERATION — "may account ba ang email na ito?" (dapat HINDI malaman ng attacker)
### 📅 Day 71 · Phase 15 (Huwag ibunyag kung sino ang may account)
### =========================================================================
### Bakit mahalaga: ang listahan ng mga email na MAY account ang unang hakbang ng attacker —
###   iyon lang ang huhulaan ng password, o padadalhan ng pekeng "i-reset ang password mo" (phishing).
###
### Paano ikumpara: ang bawat pares sa ibaba ay parehong request — isa sa email na MAY account, isa sa WALA.
###   Dapat PAREHO ang status, ang body, at ang headers (hal. Retry-After).
###
### Day 71: ang email na walang account ay may sariling bilang na rin (unknown_login_attempts, hash lang ng email),
###   kaya pareho na ang 401 ×5 → 423. Dati: laging 401 ang walang account → 6 na mali lang, alam na kung sino ang may account.
### ⚠️ Natitirang butas (alam, hindi inayos): ang REGISTER ay 409 "Email already registered" (#9). Ang tanging tunay na ayos ay
###   "email-first signup" (laging "tingnan ang email mo", account lang pagkatapos ng link) — pagbabago ng UX. Nililimitahan ng rate limit.
###
### Sa dev: bagong server (10 palpak na login bawat IP — 7 ang ginagamit dito). Ang #2–#6 ay gumagawa ng row sa
###   unknown_login_attempts: sa loob ng 15 minuto, 423 na agad ang ulit. Para ulitin agad:
###     docker exec auth-learning-postgres-1 psql -U auth -d auth_learning -c "delete from unknown_login_attempts"  (dev lang)
### Code: backend/src/routes/auth.ts (/auth/login) · lib/loginLockout.ts (unknownEmailCounter) · db/schema.ts
### Test: routes/enumeration.test.ts · Diagram: docs/diagrams/04-login-flow.md
### =========================================================================

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 0. Account (isang beses lang — 409 kung mayroon na)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "enum-demo@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. MAY account, maling password. Ang inaasahan: 401 { "error": "Invalid email or password" }
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "enum-demo@example.com", "password": "mali" }

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. WALANG account. Ang inaasahan: 401 — EKSAKTONG parehong body ng #1
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "walang-account-enum-demo@example.com", "password": "mali" }

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3–5. WALANG account, tatlo pa. Ang inaasahan: 401 × 3
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "walang-account-enum-demo@example.com", "password": "mali-2" }

###
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "walang-account-enum-demo@example.com", "password": "mali-3" }

###
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "walang-account-enum-demo@example.com", "password": "mali-4" }

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. WALANG account, ang ikalima. Ang inaasahan: 401 (at ngayon "naka-lock" na ang email na ito)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "walang-account-enum-demo@example.com", "password": "mali-5" }

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. WALANG account, ikaanim. Ang inaasahan: 423 { "error": "Account temporarily locked. Please try again later." }
###    + Retry-After: 900 — PAREHO ng totoong account sa 21-lockout.http #2 (dati: 401 dito → nabubunyag)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "walang-account-enum-demo@example.com", "password": "mali-6" }

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 8a/8b. Forgot password — may account at wala. Ang inaasahan: 202 at PAREHONG mensahe (mula Day 59)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "enum-demo@example.com" }

###
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "walang-account-enum-demo@example.com" }

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 9. ⚠️ Ang natitirang butas: register ng email na MAY account. Ang inaasahan: 409 { "error": "Email already registered" }
###    (walang account → 201). Tingnan ang paliwanag sa itaas.
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "enum-demo@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}
